Subject: [PATCH] docs(models): match GPT-6 effort, autoraise and no-disable
 docs to the code

Three docs lag the GPT-6 / GPT-6.1 model handling on main:

- context-compression-and-caching.md (codex_gpt55_autoraise row and the
  "Codex gpt-5.x / Astra threshold autoraise" section) named only gpt-6
  Astra. _is_codex_gpt54_or_gpt55() also prefix-matches gpt-6-sol,
  gpt-6-luna and gpt-6.1-sol on openai-codex, so those get the 272K cap and
  the 85% autoraise too. Its docstring listed a "Terra" GPT-6 tier the
  predicate does not match (GPT6_TIER_PREFIXES is sol/luna only); drop it and
  name gpt-6.1 Sol.
- configuration.md reasoning-mandatory note said a thinking-off auxiliary
  call is always lifted to `low`. That holds when the catalog marks the
  model mandatory or the route already refused a disable
  (agent/auxiliary_reasoning_floor.py). On OpenRouter, an openai/ model whose
  built-in ladder lacks `none` (gpt-6.1-sol, whose catalog wrongly lists
  `none`) instead has the reasoning field omitted
  (openrouter _clamp_reasoning_to_catalog -> None), so it runs at its own
  default effort.
- providers.md said `max` is "gpt-5.6-only" on an api.openai.com custom
  entry. codex_supported_efforts() also offers `max` for gpt-6 Sol/Luna
  (CODEX_GPT56_EFFORTS) and Astra / gpt-6.1 Sol (CODEX_ASTRA_EFFORTS).
